      "hints": [
        "Find the $x^3$ term in $(1 - px)^5$: $\\binom{5}{3}(1)^2(-px)^3 = -10p^3 x^3$.",
        "Equate $-10p^3 = -2160$ and solve for $p$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Identify the general term in the binomial expansion of $(1 - px)^5$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{5}{r}(1)^{5-r}(-px)^r$$",
        "Set $r = 3$ to find the term in $x^3$:\n$$\\text{Term in } x^3 = \\binom{5}{3}(-px)^3 = 10(-p^3 x^3) = -10p^3 x^3$$",
        "Equate the coefficient to $-2160$ and solve for the constant $p$:\n$$-10p^3 = -2160 \\implies p^3 = 216 \\implies p = \\sqrt[3]{216} = 6$$"
      ],
